diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 31b0fae..4ada6b8 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -5,3 +5,16 @@ A repository that runs its tests on every pull request.
 ## Contributing
 
 Open a pull request. Contributions arrive from forks.
+
+## Triage
+
+`.github/workflows/triage.yml` runs when a pull request is opened. It comments
+to welcome the contributor by username, repeating the pull request title as a
+summary, and applies the `needs-triage` label. The label must already exist in
+the repository.
+
+Because contributions arrive from forks, the workflow uses `pull_request_target`,
+which runs with a write-capable token even for fork pull requests. This is safe
+only because the workflow never checks out or runs the pull request's code, and
+passes the title and username to the shell through environment variables. Keep
+it that way: do not add a checkout of the pull request head to this workflow.
